## Tests

`apps/web/src/highlight.test.ts` (new). Each test builds `const index = split(code("index.css"), COARSE)`, then `pageRules = rulesIn(index.outside)` and `coarseRules = index.inside.flatMap(rulesIn)`. `rulesIn(index.outside)` is every rule outside any `@media`, so a match proves "at every pointer".

- `it("#3260 html takes no tap highlight, at every pointer")`: `bodyOf(pageRules, "html")` matches `/-webkit-tap-highlight-color:\s*transparent;/`.
- `it("#3260 html selects as ever at a fine pointer")`: `index.inside.length > 0`, and `bodyOf(pageRules, "html")` matches neither `user-select` nor `touch-callout`.
- `it("#3260 under a coarse pointer html takes no selection and no callout")`: `bodyOf(coarseRules, "html")` matches `-webkit-touch-callout: none;`, `-webkit-user-select: none;` and `UNPREFIXED_SELECT("none")`.
- `it("#3260 under a coarse pointer an input, a textarea and a contenteditable take their text back")`:
  - `fields = coarseRules.filter((rule) => UNPREFIXED_SELECT("text").test(rule.body))` is non-empty.
  - The joined selectors contain `input`, `textarea` and `[contenteditable`.
  - The joined bodies match `-webkit-user-select: text;`.
- `it("#3260 .chat-panel gives the tap highlight, the callout and the selection back")`: `bodyOf(rulesIn(split(code(CHAT_SHEET), COARSE).outside), ".chat-panel")` matches `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: initial;`, `-webkit-touch-callout: default;`, `-webkit-user-select: text;` and `UNPREFIXED_SELECT("text")`.
