## Done when

- [ ] `html` takes no tap highlight at any pointer.
- [ ] Under `(pointer: coarse)`, `html` takes `user-select: none` and `-webkit-touch-callout: none`, and fields take `user-select: text`.
- [ ] `.chat-panel` restores all three.
- [ ] `board.css` sets no tap highlight, and the #2015 zone rules are gone.
- [ ] The 2FA key's `-webkit-user-select: all` is in.
- [ ] `highlight.test.ts` is green, including the stylesheet lint tests (`palette`, `typescale`, `surfaces`, `motion`, `cursors`, `typography`).
- [ ] The full `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, typecheck and eslint on the touched test files are green.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `catalog check`, `patches check`, `spec check`, clippy, cargo tests and the `wire` cleanliness test.
- [ ] The phone check ran, or the final message says it did not.
- [ ] README paragraph added.

## Risks

- `cursors.test.ts` slices `index.css` between `@media (pointer: fine)` and the first `html {`, and requires the exact `html {\n  cursor: var(--cursor-glove, auto);\n}`. Keep both untouched and put the new rules after l.446.
