# Plan (sonnet, medium)

**Goal.** On a phone the web client highlights nothing but the chat. `html` takes no tap flash at any pointer. Under `(pointer: coarse)` it takes no text selection and no long-press callout. Fields (`input`, `textarea`, `contenteditable`) keep selection. `.chat-panel` restores all three. The #2015 zone rule in `board.css` goes, because its `initial` on a zone's children would bring the flash back on cards. A new unit test pins all of it.

The draft commit `origin/claude/mobile-no-highlight` (8c423ffa8b) is right. Read it with `git show origin/claude/mobile-no-highlight:<path>`, but do not check it out or switch branches. This plan reuses its CSS and moves its test into a new file. It adds one thing the draft misses (step 4).

## Files to touch

| File | | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/index.css` | change | Add an `html` tap-highlight rule and a `@media (pointer: coarse)` block, after the hit-area `@media` block (the one ending just before `:where(button, input, a):focus-visible`) |
| `apps/web/src/together/together.css` | change | `.chat-panel` gives the tap highlight, the callout and the selection back |
| `apps/web/src/game/board.css` | change | Delete the #2015 comment and its two `.zone:not([data-legal="true"])` rules (~l.1104–1114) |
| `apps/web/src/auth/two-step.css` | change | `.account-two-step__secret` gets `-webkit-user-select: all;` |
| `apps/web/src/highlight.test.ts` | new | The stylesheet test |
| `apps/web/src/game/Zone.test.tsx` | change | Drop the old CSS test, its three imports and the header's mention of it |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | One paragraph after the hit-area paragraph |

Do not touch `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `.claude/`, `crates/`, `spec/` or `e2e/`. No spec section or ruling governs this: the issue prescribes a presentation rule, so there is no ruling note. Do not cite an `R<n>` id in the new code (`spec check` scans for them), and do not run `cargo jackioh spec index`.

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/index.css`.** Insert this after the hit-area block. `cursors.test.ts` slices from `@media (pointer: fine)` to the first `html {` (l.105), so the new rules must stay below it.
   ```css
   /* No highlighting on a phone but in the chat (#3260): … (3–6 lines: tap flash at every pointer, since only touch
      browsers draw one; selection and callout under a coarse pointer, so a narrow desktop window still selects;
      fields keep their text, since iOS will not type into or place a caret in one that cannot be selected;
      together/together.css gives the chat panel all three back) */
   html {
     -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
   }

   @media (pointer: coarse) {
     html {
       -webkit-touch-callout: none;
       -webkit-user-select: none;
       user-select: none;
     }

     :where(input, textarea, [contenteditable]:not([contenteditable="false"])) {
       -webkit-user-select: text;
       user-select: text;
     }
   }
   ```
   Keep the existing `html { cursor: … }` rule untouched: `cursors.test.ts` pins it byte for byte.

2. **`apps/web/src/together/together.css`.** In the `.chat-panel` rule (~l.193), after `box-shadow: 0 10px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 55%);`, add a one-line comment ("the one place a phone highlights (index.css): a message can be pressed, selected and copied") and:
   ```css
   -webkit-tap-highlight-color: initial;
   -webkit-touch-callout: default;
   -webkit-user-select: text;
   user-select: text;
   ```
   Do not put these inside a media query.

3. **`apps/web/src/game/board.css`.** Delete the block from `/* #2015: a zone the player cannot pick now draws no tap highlight.` through the closing `}` of `.zone:not([data-legal="true"]) > * { … }`. Leave one blank line between the `cursor: var(--cursor-glove-point, pointer);` rule and `.zone[data-selected="true"]`. Leave the other stylesheets' `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` lines (`portrait.css`, `audio.css`, `deckbuilder.css`, `inspect.css`) alone: they are redundant but harmless.

4. **`apps/web/src/auth/two-step.css`.** In `.tavern.app-shell .account-two-step__secret`, add `-webkit-user-select: all;` on the line before `user-select: all;`.
   - **Why:** the 2FA key (`TwoStepSettings.tsx`) has no copy button, and Safari reads only the prefixed property. Under step 1 an iPhone would inherit `none` and the key could no longer be copied.
   - Chrome and Firefox already honor the unprefixed `all`. This is the one deliberate exception to "nothing but the chat" (see Open questions).

